    "p_value_interpretation": "A finite-sample rank position among pre-treatment reference blocks under the same forecast machinery. With K reference blocks the smallest attainable value is 1/(K+1). The primary reporting resolution cannot reach 0.05, and no cell at any resolution may be described as significant at the 5% level.",
    "reference_blocks_are_treated_units": false,
    "resolution_floor_policy": "A shorter block length packs more blocks into the same fixed pre-period and therefore mechanically lowers the 1/(K+1) floor without adding any observation, while shortening the accumulation each block measures and weakening block independence. Finer-resolution floors are reported for completeness only. The reporting resolution is fixed at primary_horizon_days by this file and must never be replaced by whichever horizon produced the smallest floor.",
    "unbounded_interval_policy": "When the required order statistic exceeds K the conformal radius is infinite and the interval is reported as unbounded. Clipping the rank to K would silently understate the requested coverage and is prohibited."
